{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"motionMirroring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftGodotRuntime7Vector2V","text":"Vector2","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you want the repetition to pixel-perfect match a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Texture2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" displayed by a child node, you should account for any scale applied to the texture when defining this interval. For example, if you use a child "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Sprite2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" scaled to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.5"},{"type":"text","text":" to display a 600x600 texture, and want this sprite to be repeated continuously horizontally, you should set the mirroring to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vector2(300, 0)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"Note"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the length of the viewport axis is bigger than twice the repeated axis size, it will not repeat infinitely, as the parallax layer only draws 2 instances of the layer at any given time. The visibility window is calculated from the parent "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ParallaxBackground","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s position, not the layer’s own position. So, if you use mirroring, "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"do not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" change the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ParallaxLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" position relative to its parent. Instead, if you need to adjust the background’s position, set the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CanvasLayer\/offset","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" property in the parent "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ParallaxBackground","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"Note"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Despite the name, the layer will not be mirrored, it will only be repeated."}]}],"name":"Note"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/parallaxlayer\/motionmirroring"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The interval, in pixels, at which the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ParallaxLayer"},{"type":"text","text":" is drawn repeatedly. Useful for creating an infinitely scrolling background. If an axis is set to "},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ParallaxLayer"},{"type":"text","text":" will be drawn only once along that direction."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ParallaxLayer"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot13ParallaxLayerC15motionMirroring0aB7Runtime7Vector2Vvp","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"fragme